+              Ian made landfall in southwestern Florida at category 4 intensity (on the Saffir-Simpson Hurricane Wind
+      Scale), producing catastrophic storm surge, damaging winds, and historic freshwater flooding across much of
+      central and northern Florida. Ian was responsible for over 150 direct and indirect deaths and over $112 billion
+      in damage, making it the costliest hurricane in Florida’s history and the third-costliest in United States history.
+      Ian also made landfall as a category 3 hurricane in western Cuba bringing widespread damage and loss of
+      power to the entire island. Ian made its final landfall as a category 1 hurricane in South Carolina.
